IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ja-juror`

-- Juries Act 1957 (WA) -- the Q&A layer: the questions people ask, with the seat and the situation as parameters, so
-- that one deployment serves every seat and the question form drops the questions that do not arise.
--
-- SEATS (`my role`, the first input of every exported question, "Which of these describes you"):
--   * the person liable for jury service, or summonsed for it -- the baseline's seat (Chloe, c025 and c077), whose 30
--     questions are asked here by calling the baseline's functions in ja-juror.l4;
--   * the employer of a person summonsed -- bound by s 56 (no prejudicial action, or threat of it, over the summons or
--     jury service; the earnings to keep paying), paid the fees under s 58B(3) if it keeps paying, and unable to excuse
--     (ss 34F-34J).
-- A question about another role answers `does not arise for you` without reading any other input. The sheriff, the
-- summoning officer, the jury pool supervisor, the judge and the State as payer are never seats: what they may or must
-- do appears as what it means for the person asking.
--
-- SITUATIONS (design D8 of the graffiti encoding): within a role, a question that arises only in a situation takes that
-- situation's fact straight after `my role`, and when it does not hold answers `does not arise for you` without reading
-- anything else. The questions of one situation share one input, character for character. All are BOOLEAN, FALSE
-- being the value that does not hold:
--   * `I have been served with a jury summons` (the person): the questions of answering the summons, excusal on a
--     ground of ss 34G-34J, service, attendance, and s 55;
--   * `I have attended to serve, or served, as a juror` (the person): the s 58B payments and the s 56B confidentiality
--     questions, which the Act ties to jury service done;
--   * `I work for an employer` (the person): the s 56 questions about what the employer did, the earnings and the fine;
--   * `my employer has been convicted under s 56(5)` (the person) and `I have been convicted under s 56(5)` (the
--     employer): compensation and re-employment, which s 56(7) ties to the conviction.
-- A question that arises in every situation of its role (liability, eligibility, qualification and standing; the
-- permanent excusal certificate; whether I am doing jury service; the employer's own s 56 and s 58B questions, the role
-- being an employer of a person summonsed) takes no situation input.
--
-- No exported question takes a DEONTIC or EVENT input. The baseline's records (`Person`, `Circumstances`) are taken as
-- the baseline takes them.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md, "Q&A layer (seat and situations as parameters)".

§ `Juries Act 1957 (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I am liable for jury service, or have been summonsed for it`
    `I employ someone who has been summonsed for jury service`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

DECLARE `Amount` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    amount HAS dollars IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Items to disclose` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    items HAS `the item numbers of Schedule 2` IS A LIST OF NUMBER

-- The person's answers that are the baseline's own enumerations, carried with `does not arise for you`.
DECLARE `Standing, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A Standing

DECLARE `Good reason outcome, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A GoodReasonOutcome

DECLARE `Attendance, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS AN AttendAnswer

DECLARE `Fee recipient, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A FeeRecipient

-- What the employer did, in the employer's words; `in the employee's words` gives the baseline's EmployerAction.
DECLARE `What I did to my employee` IS ONE OF
    `I end their employment`
    `I stop paying them`
    `I cut their pay`
    `I otherwise prejudice them in their employment`
    `I threaten to end their employment, cut or stop their pay or otherwise prejudice them`
    `I do not pay them the earnings they could reasonably expect while on jury service`
    `I threaten not to pay them those earnings`
    `I tell them they cannot go, but threaten nothing and do nothing`
    `I do nothing adverse`

§§ `Helpers`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

-- Lists every value, with no OTHERWISE (graffiti finding 31).
GIVEN `what I did` IS A `What I did to my employee`
GIVETH AN EmployerAction
`in the employee's words` `what I did` MEANS
    CONSIDER `what I did`
    WHEN `I end their employment` THEN `ends my employment`
    WHEN `I stop paying them` THEN `stops paying me`
    WHEN `I cut their pay` THEN `cuts my pay`
    WHEN `I otherwise prejudice them in their employment` THEN `otherwise prejudices me in my employment`
    WHEN `I threaten to end their employment, cut or stop their pay or otherwise prejudice them` THEN `threatens to end my employment or cut or stop my pay or otherwise prejudice me`
    WHEN `I do not pay them the earnings they could reasonably expect while on jury service` THEN `does not pay me the earnings I could reasonably expect while on jury service`
    WHEN `I threaten not to pay them those earnings` THEN `threatens not to pay me those earnings`
    WHEN `I tell them they cannot go, but threaten nothing and do nothing` THEN `tells me I cannot go but threatens nothing and does nothing`
    WHEN `I do nothing adverse` THEN `nothing adverse`

§§ `For the person liable for jury service or summonsed (the baseline's seat)`

-- Each question calls the baseline's function of the same subject (ja-juror.l4) and restates no rule: for this role,
-- and where its situation holds, its answer is the baseline's, carried in the answer types above.

§§§ `ss 4, 5, Sch 1 -- am I liable, eligible and qualified`

@export Am I liable to serve on a jury in Western Australia (Juries Act 1957 (WA) s 4)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS A Person @desc Your enrolment, age, Schedule 1 class, criminal record and legal status
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I liable to serve on a jury in Western Australia` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am liable for jury service, or have been summonsed for it` THEN `yes if` (`Am I liable to serve as a juror` `me`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I eligible to serve on a jury at this kind of trial (Juries Act 1957 (WA) s 5(3)(a), (ba), (bb), Sch 1)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS A Person @desc Your enrolment, age, Schedule 1 class, criminal record and legal status
      `trial` IS A TrialKind @desc The kind of trial: "a criminal trial" or "a civil trial"
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I eligible to serve on a jury at this kind of trial` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am liable for jury service, or have been summonsed for it` THEN `yes if` (`Am I eligible to serve` `me` `trial`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Does my criminal record disqualify me from jury service (Juries Act 1957 (WA) s 5(3)(b))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS A Person @desc Your enrolment, age, Schedule 1 class, criminal record and legal status
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does my criminal record disqualify me from jury service` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am liable for jury service, or have been summonsed for it` THEN `yes if` (`Does my criminal record disqualify me` `me`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I qualified to serve on a jury (Juries Act 1957 (WA) s 5(3)(b), (c), (d))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS A Person @desc Your enrolment, age, Schedule 1 class, criminal record and legal status
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I qualified to serve on a jury` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am liable for jury service, or have been summonsed for it` THEN `yes if` (`Am I qualified to serve` `me`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Where do I stand for jury service at this kind of trial: not liable, not eligible, not qualified, or liable to serve unless excused (Juries Act 1957 (WA) ss 4, 5)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS A Person @desc Your enrolment, age, Schedule 1 class, criminal record and legal status
      `trial` IS A TrialKind @desc The kind of trial: "a criminal trial" or "a civil trial"
GIVETH A `Standing, if it arises`
`Where do I stand for jury service at this kind of trial` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am liable for jury service, or have been summonsed for it` THEN `the answer is` (`What is my standing for this trial` `me` `trial`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 33A, Sch 2, ss 34E-34J -- answering the summons, and being excused`

@export Which items of Schedule 2 must I disclose to the summoning officer or the court (Juries Act 1957 (WA) s 33A, Sch 2)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been served with a jury summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a jury summons has been served on you (the questions about answering it, being excused, attending and not obeying arise only then)
      `me` IS A Person @desc Your enrolment, age, Schedule 1 class, criminal record and legal status
      `trial` IS A TrialKind @desc The kind of trial: "a criminal trial" or "a civil trial"
      `mine` IS A Circumstances @desc Your other circumstances that bear on excusal
GIVETH AN `Items to disclose`
`Which items of Schedule 2 must I disclose when I answer my summons` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am liable for jury service, or have been summonsed for it` THEN
        IF `I have been served with a jury summons`
        THEN `items` (`Which Schedule 2 items must I disclose` `me` `trial` `mine`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must I be excused from my summons, if the judge or summoning officer is satisfied of the ground (Juries Act 1957 (WA) s 34G)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been served with a jury summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a jury summons has been served on you (the questions about answering it, being excused, attending and not obeying arise only then)
      `me` IS A Person @desc Your enrolment, age, Schedule 1 class, criminal record and legal status
      `trial` IS A TrialKind @desc The kind of trial: "a criminal trial" or "a civil trial"
      `mine` IS A Circumstances @desc Your other circumstances that bear on excusal
      `the judge or summoning officer is satisfied of the ground` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the judge or summoning officer is satisfied that the ground applies to you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I be excused from my summons on a ground of s 34G` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am liable for jury service, or have been summonsed for it` THEN
        IF `I have been served with a jury summons`
        THEN `yes if` (`Must I be excused` `me` `trial` `mine` `the judge or summoning officer is satisfied of the ground`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can my employer excuse me from my jury summons (Juries Act 1957 (WA) ss 34F-34J)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been served with a jury summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a jury summons has been served on you (the questions about answering it, being excused, attending and not obeying arise only then)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can my employer excuse me from my summons` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am liable for jury service, or have been summonsed for it` THEN
        IF `I have been served with a jury summons`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can my employer excuse me`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can the sheriff give me a certificate permanently excusing me from jury service (Juries Act 1957 (WA) s 34E)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the sheriff is satisfied I am permanently incapable because of a physical disability or mental impairment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the sheriff is satisfied you are permanently incapable of serving effectively because of a physical disability or mental impairment
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I get a certificate permanently excusing me from jury service` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am liable for jury service, or have been summonsed for it` THEN `yes if` (`Can I get a permanent excusal certificate` `the sheriff is satisfied I am permanently incapable because of a physical disability or mental impairment`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can I take my application to be excused to a judge (Juries Act 1957 (WA) s 34F(4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been served with a jury summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a jury summons has been served on you (the questions about answering it, being excused, attending and not obeying arise only then)
      `the summoning officer refused my application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the summoning officer has refused your application to be excused
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I take my application to be excused to a judge` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am liable for jury service, or have been summonsed for it` THEN
        IF `I have been served with a jury summons`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can I renew my application before a judge` `the summoning officer refused my application`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Do I have a good reason to be excused from my summons (Juries Act 1957 (WA) s 34H(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been served with a jury summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a jury summons has been served on you (the questions about answering it, being excused, attending and not obeying arise only then)
      `cause` IS A GoodReasonCause @desc What makes attendance hard: "my business or occupation", "a special or pressing commitment", "a mental impairment", "a physical disability", "my physical health", "other personal circumstances" or "no particular cause"
      `attending would cause undue hardship or serious inconvenience to me, my family or the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether attending as summoned would cause undue hardship or serious inconvenience to you, your family or the general public
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Do I have a good reason to be excused from my summons` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am liable for jury service, or have been summonsed for it` THEN
        IF `I have been served with a jury summons`
        THEN `yes if` (`Do I have a good reason` `cause` `attending would cause undue hardship or serious inconvenience to me, my family or the public`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What can I get by applying to be excused for good reason: a deferral, an excusal, or nothing (Juries Act 1957 (WA) s 34H)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been served with a jury summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a jury summons has been served on you (the questions about answering it, being excused, attending and not obeying arise only then)
      `I have applied to be excused for good reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have applied to the summoning officer or a judge to be excused for good reason (s 34H)
      `the officer is satisfied I have a good reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the judge or summoning officer is satisfied you have a good reason (s 34H(2))
      `this summons follows an earlier deferral` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this summons was issued because you were granted a deferral before
      `the reason was not reasonably foreseeable at the earlier deferral` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your reason could not reasonably have been foreseen when the earlier deferral was granted
      `there are exceptional reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the officer accepts there are exceptional reasons to excuse you again
GIVETH A `Good reason outcome, if it arises`
`What can I get by applying to be excused for good reason` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am liable for jury service, or have been summonsed for it` THEN
        IF `I have been served with a jury summons`
        THEN `the answer is` (`What can I get for a good reason` `I have applied to be excused for good reason` `the officer is satisfied I have a good reason` `this summons follows an earlier deferral` `the reason was not reasonably foreseeable at the earlier deferral` `there are exceptional reasons`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must I be excused from a trial because I would not be indifferent between the parties (Juries Act 1957 (WA) s 34I)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been served with a jury summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a jury summons has been served on you (the questions about answering it, being excused, attending and not obeying arise only then)
      `who` IS A Decider @desc Who is deciding: "the summoning officer" or "a judge"
      `I have applied to be excused for not being indifferent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have applied to be excused because you would not be indifferent between the parties (s 34I)
      `they are satisfied I would not be indifferent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the judge or summoning officer is satisfied you would not be indifferent between the parties
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I be excused from a trial because I would not be indifferent` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am liable for jury service, or have been summonsed for it` THEN
        IF `I have been served with a jury summons`
        THEN `yes if` (`Must I be excused for not being indifferent` `who` `I have applied to be excused for not being indifferent` `they are satisfied I would not be indifferent`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can I be excused because I attended or served as a juror in WA in the last 5 years (Juries Act 1957 (WA) s 34J)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been served with a jury summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a jury summons has been served on you (the questions about answering it, being excused, attending and not obeying arise only then)
      `I have applied to be excused for recent jury service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have applied to be excused because you attended or served as a juror in WA in the last 5 years (s 34J)
      `I attended or served as a juror in WA in the 5 years before my first attendance date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, under an earlier summons, you attended to serve or served as a juror in WA in the 5 years before the first date this summons requires you to attend
      `enough other summoned people are present` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether enough other summoned people are present to choose the jurors
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I be excused because I served on a jury in the last 5 years` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am liable for jury service, or have been summonsed for it` THEN
        IF `I have been served with a jury summons`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can I be excused for recent service` `I have applied to be excused for recent jury service` `I attended or served as a juror in WA in the 5 years before my first attendance date` `enough other summoned people are present`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 31, 32D, 32I, 42, 55 -- service, attendance, and not obeying`

@export Was my jury summons served on me in time (Juries Act 1957 (WA) s 31 for a panel, s 32D(2) for a jury pool)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been served with a jury summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a jury summons has been served on you (the questions about answering it, being excused, attending and not obeying arise only then)
      `kind` IS A SummonsKind @desc "a summons to a panel" or "a summons to a jury pool"
      `days from service to attendance` IS A NUMBER @desc Days from the day the summons was served on you (for a posted summons, the day it would arrive in the ordinary course of post) to the day you must attend; for example served on the 1st to attend on the 8th is 7
      `a judge ordered that I attend despite late service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a judge ordered that you attend a jury pool although the summons was served late
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Was my jury summons served on me in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am liable for jury service, or have been summonsed for it` THEN
        IF `I have been served with a jury summons`
        THEN `yes if` (`Was my summons served in time` `kind` `days from service to attendance` `a judge ordered that I attend despite late service`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must I attend as my jury summons says (Juries Act 1957 (WA) ss 31, 32D, 32E, 32I, 34G)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been served with a jury summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a jury summons has been served on you (the questions about answering it, being excused, attending and not obeying arise only then)
      `me` IS A Person @desc Your enrolment, age, Schedule 1 class, criminal record and legal status
      `trial` IS A TrialKind @desc The kind of trial: "a criminal trial" or "a civil trial"
      `kind` IS A SummonsKind @desc "a summons to a panel" or "a summons to a jury pool"
      `days from service to attendance` IS A NUMBER @desc Days from the day the summons was served on you (for a posted summons, the day it would arrive in the ordinary course of post) to the day you must attend; for example served on the 1st to attend on the 8th is 7
      `a judge ordered that I attend despite late service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a judge ordered that you attend a jury pool although the summons was served late
      `I have been excused or deferred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a judge or the summoning officer has excused you or deferred your jury duty
      `my summons was withdrawn or I was discharged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the summoning officer withdrew your summons (s 32E) or discharged you from the pool (s 32I(3))
GIVETH AN `Attendance, if it arises`
`Must I attend as my jury summons says` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am liable for jury service, or have been summonsed for it` THEN
        IF `I have been served with a jury summons`
        THEN `the answer is` (`Must I attend` `me` `trial` `kind` `days from service to attendance` `a judge ordered that I attend despite late service` `I have been excused or deferred` `my summons was withdrawn or I was discharged`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can I be required to attend on this day of my jury service (Juries Act 1957 (WA) ss 32I, 42)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been served with a jury summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a jury summons has been served on you (the questions about answering it, being excused, attending and not obeying arise only then)
      `kind` IS A SummonsKind @desc "a summons to a panel" or "a summons to a jury pool"
      `which day of attendance this is` IS A NUMBER @desc Which court sitting day of your attendance this would be (1 for the first day)
      `the pool period set by the summoning officer` IS A NUMBER @desc For a jury pool, the number of consecutive court sitting days the summoning officer set (at most 5); for a panel, enter 5
      `I am on a jury whose trial is not finished` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been sworn on a jury whose case is still going
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I be required to attend on this day of my jury service` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am liable for jury service, or have been summonsed for it` THEN
        IF `I have been served with a jury summons`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can I be required to attend today` `kind` `which day of attendance this is` `the pool period set by the summoning officer` `I am on a jury whose trial is not finished`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Do I commit an offence if I do not obey my jury summons (Juries Act 1957 (WA) s 55(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been served with a jury summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a jury summons has been served on you (the questions about answering it, being excused, attending and not obeying arise only then)
      `my summons was served as the Act requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your summons was served on you as the Act requires
      `I did not obey it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you did not attend or otherwise did not do what the summons required
      `I had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court would accept you had a reasonable excuse
      `I had been excused, deferred or discharged, or the summons was withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were excused or deferred, discharged from the pool, or told the summons was withdrawn
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Do I commit an offence if I do not obey my jury summons` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am liable for jury service, or have been summonsed for it` THEN
        IF `I have been served with a jury summons`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is not obeying my summons an offence` `my summons was served as the Act requires` `I did not obey it` `I had a reasonable excuse` `I had been excused, deferred or discharged, or the summons was withdrawn`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most I can be fined for not obeying my jury summons (Juries Act 1957 (WA) s 55)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been served with a jury summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a jury summons has been served on you (the questions about answering it, being excused, attending and not obeying arise only then)
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most I can be fined for not obeying my jury summons` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am liable for jury service, or have been summonsed for it` THEN
        IF `I have been served with a jury summons`
        THEN `amount` (`What is the most I can be fined for not obeying`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 56, 58B -- my employer, and what I am paid`

@export Am I doing jury service within the Act (Juries Act 1957 (WA) ss 56(4), 58B(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I was required under the Act to attend` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a summons or direction under the Juries Act required you to attend
      `I attend to serve or serve as a juror` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you attend any place in order to serve, or serve, as a juror
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I doing jury service within the Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am liable for jury service, or have been summonsed for it` THEN `yes if` (`Am I doing jury service` `I was required under the Act to attend` `I attend to serve or serve as a juror`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is what my employer did prejudicial action under the Juries Act (Juries Act 1957 (WA) s 56(2), (3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I work for an employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you work for someone, as an employee or under a contract for services (s 56(1))
      `act` IS AN EmployerAction @desc What your employer (or someone acting for it) did
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is what my employer did prejudicial action against me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am liable for jury service, or have been summonsed for it` THEN
        IF `I work for an employer`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is it prejudicial action` `act`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Does my employer commit an offence by what it did (Juries Act 1957 (WA) s 56(5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I work for an employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you work for someone, as an employee or under a contract for services (s 56(1))
      `act` IS AN EmployerAction @desc What your employer (or someone acting for it) did
      `I am under a jury summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are subject to a jury summons
      `I have done or am doing jury service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have attended or served, or are attending or serving, as a juror under the Act
      `my employer proves it was not because of the summons or jury service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer can prove its act was not because of your summons or jury service
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does my employer commit an offence by what it did to me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am liable for jury service, or have been summonsed for it` THEN
        IF `I work for an employer`
        THEN `yes if` (`Does my employer commit an offence` `act` `I am under a jury summons` `I have done or am doing jury service` `my employer proves it was not because of the summons or jury service`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What earnings must my employer keep paying me while I do jury service, so as not to act prejudicially (Juries Act 1957 (WA) s 56(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I work for an employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you work for someone, as an employee or under a contract for services (s 56(1))
      `days of jury service` IS A NUMBER @desc Working days away from work doing jury service
      `earnings I could reasonably expect per day` IS A NUMBER @desc What you could reasonably expect to be paid under your contract for each of those days, in dollars
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What earnings must my employer keep paying me while I do jury service` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am liable for jury service, or have been summonsed for it` THEN
        IF `I work for an employer`
        THEN `amount` (`What earnings must my employer keep paying me` `days of jury service` `earnings I could reasonably expect per day`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most my employer can be fined for acting prejudicially against me over jury service (Juries Act 1957 (WA) s 56(5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I work for an employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you work for someone, as an employee or under a contract for services (s 56(1))
      `my employer is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer is a company or other body corporate
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most my employer can be fined for acting prejudicially against me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am liable for jury service, or have been summonsed for it` THEN
        IF `I work for an employer`
        THEN `amount` (`What is the most my employer can be fined` `my employer is a body corporate`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most compensation a court can order my employer to pay me after convicting it (Juries Act 1957 (WA) s 56(7), (8))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my employer has been convicted under s 56(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court has convicted your employer of acting prejudicially against you over jury service (s 56(5))
      `my remuneration in the 12 months before the offence` IS A NUMBER @desc What you were paid by that employer in the 12 months immediately before the offence, in dollars
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most compensation a court can order my employer to pay me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am liable for jury service, or have been summonsed for it` THEN
        IF `my employer has been convicted under s 56(5)`
        THEN `amount` (`What is the most compensation I can be awarded` `my remuneration in the 12 months before the offence`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can the court order my employer to take me back (Juries Act 1957 (WA) s 56(7)(b))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my employer has been convicted under s 56(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court has convicted your employer of acting prejudicially against you over jury service (s 56(5))
      `act` IS AN EmployerAction @desc What your employer (or someone acting for it) did
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can the court order my employer to take me back` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am liable for jury service, or have been summonsed for it` THEN
        IF `my employer has been convicted under s 56(5)`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can the court order my re-employment` `my employer has been convicted under s 56(5)` `act`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Who does the State pay the jury service fees to: my employer, me, or no one (Juries Act 1957 (WA) s 58B(3)-(5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have attended to serve, or served, as a juror` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have attended a court to serve, or served, as a juror under the Act (the questions about payment and about what you may say arise only then)
      `I am employed on a contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an employee on a contract of service (not a contractor)
      `my employer pays me my usual earnings for the jury service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer pays you the earnings you could reasonably expect for the period of jury service
      `my employer is in a prescribed class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations under the Act put your employer in a class not entitled to the fees
      `I am in a prescribed class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations under the Act put you in a class not entitled to the fees
GIVETH A `Fee recipient, if it arises`
`Who does the State pay my jury service fees to` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am liable for jury service, or have been summonsed for it` THEN
        IF `I have attended to serve, or served, as a juror`
        THEN `the answer is` (`Who gets the jury service fees` `I am employed on a contract of service` `my employer pays me my usual earnings for the jury service` `my employer is in a prescribed class` `I am in a prescribed class`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- The situation is the baseline's `I do jury service`: the question arises only once I have attended or served, and
-- the baseline is called with TRUE.
@export How much does the State pay me for my jury service (Juries Act 1957 (WA) s 58B)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have attended to serve, or served, as a juror` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have attended a court to serve, or served, as a juror under the Act (the questions about payment and about what you may say arise only then)
      `prescribed allowances and expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc The allowances and expenses the regulations under the Act prescribe for your service, in dollars
      `prescribed fees` IS A NUMBER @desc The fees the regulations under the Act prescribe for your service, in dollars
      `recipient` IS A FeeRecipient @desc Who the fees go to: "my employer", "me" or "no one -- a prescribed class"
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much does the State pay me for my jury service` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am liable for jury service, or have been summonsed for it` THEN
        IF `I have attended to serve, or served, as a juror`
        THEN `amount` (`How much does the State pay me` TRUE `prescribed allowances and expenses` `prescribed fees` `recipient`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 56A, 56B, 56E -- what I may say about the jury`

@export Is it an offence for me to tell this about my jury (Juries Act 1957 (WA) ss 56A, 56B, 56E)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have attended to serve, or served, as a juror` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have attended a court to serve, or served, as a juror under the Act (the questions about payment and about what you may say arise only then)
      `what` IS A WhatITell @desc What you would tell
      `whom` IS A WhoITell @desc Who you would tell
      `I know it will or is likely to be published` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are aware that, because you tell it, it will or is likely to reach the public
      `the trial is over` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the trial has been completed
      `the court gave leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court gave leave to identify the juror during the trial
      `the other juror consents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other person named as a juror consents
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is it an offence for me to tell this about my jury` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am liable for jury service, or have been summonsed for it` THEN
        IF `I have attended to serve, or served, as a juror`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is telling it an offence` `what` `whom` `I know it will or is likely to be published` `the trial is over` `the court gave leave` `the other juror consents`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most I can be fined for disclosing protected jury information (Juries Act 1957 (WA) s 56B)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have attended to serve, or served, as a juror` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have attended a court to serve, or served, as a juror under the Act (the questions about payment and about what you may say arise only then)
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most I can be fined for disclosing protected jury information` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am liable for jury service, or have been summonsed for it` THEN
        IF `I have attended to serve, or served, as a juror`
        THEN `amount` (`What is the most I can be fined for disclosing`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the employer of a person summonsed for jury service (ss 34F-34J, 56, 58B)`

-- s 56(1): "employer includes a person acting on behalf of an employer" and "employee includes a person employed under
-- a contract for services". s 56(2), (3), (5): the employer must not act prejudicially, or threaten to, because the
-- employee is under a summons or doing jury service; not paying the earnings the employee could reasonably expect
-- while doing jury service is prejudicial. s 58B(3): an employer that keeps paying an employee on a contract of
-- service gets the fees, unless it is in a prescribed class. ss 34F-34J name only a judge and the summoning officer
-- as able to excuse. Each question calls the baseline's function, with the employer's act put in the baseline's words.

§§§ `ss 34F-34J -- excusal`

@export May I excuse my employee from their jury summons (Juries Act 1957 (WA) ss 34F-34J)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I excuse my employee from jury service` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ someone who has been summonsed for jury service` THEN `yes if` (`Can my employer excuse me`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 56 -- what I may not do`

@export Is what I did, or would do, prejudicial action against my employee over jury service (Juries Act 1957 (WA) s 56(2), (3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what I did` IS A `What I did to my employee` @desc What you, or someone acting for you, did or would do to the employee
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is what I did prejudicial action against my employee` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ someone who has been summonsed for jury service` THEN `yes if` (`Is it prejudicial action` (`in the employee's words` `what I did`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Do I commit an offence by what I did to my employee (Juries Act 1957 (WA) s 56(5), (6))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what I did` IS A `What I did to my employee` @desc What you, or someone acting for you, did or would do to the employee
      `my employee is under a jury summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employee is subject to a jury summons
      `my employee has done or is doing jury service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employee has attended or served, or is attending or serving, as a juror under the Act
      `I can prove it was not because of the summons or jury service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can prove your act was not because of the summons or the jury service
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Do I commit an offence by what I did to my employee` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ someone who has been summonsed for jury service` THEN `yes if` (`Does my employer commit an offence` (`in the employee's words` `what I did`) `my employee is under a jury summons` `my employee has done or is doing jury service` `I can prove it was not because of the summons or jury service`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What earnings must I keep paying my employee while they do jury service, so as not to act prejudicially (Juries Act 1957 (WA) s 56(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `days of jury service` IS A NUMBER @desc Working days away from work doing jury service
      `earnings the employee could reasonably expect per day` IS A NUMBER @desc What the employee could reasonably expect to be paid for each of those days, in dollars
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What earnings must I keep paying my employee while they do jury service` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ someone who has been summonsed for jury service` THEN `amount` (`What earnings must my employer keep paying me` `days of jury service` `earnings the employee could reasonably expect per day`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most I can be fined for acting prejudicially against my employee over jury service (Juries Act 1957 (WA) s 56(5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a company or other body corporate
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most I can be fined for acting prejudicially against my employee` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ someone who has been summonsed for jury service` THEN `amount` (`What is the most my employer can be fined` `I am a body corporate`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most compensation a court can order me to pay my employee after convicting me (Juries Act 1957 (WA) s 56(7), (8))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been convicted under s 56(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court has convicted you of acting prejudicially against your employee over jury service (s 56(5))
      `the employee's remuneration in the 12 months before the offence` IS A NUMBER @desc What you paid the employee in the 12 months immediately before the offence, in dollars
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most compensation a court can order me to pay my employee` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ someone who has been summonsed for jury service` THEN
        IF `I have been convicted under s 56(5)`
        THEN `amount` (`What is the most compensation I can be awarded` `the employee's remuneration in the 12 months before the offence`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can the court order me to take my employee back (Juries Act 1957 (WA) s 56(7)(b))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been convicted under s 56(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court has convicted you of acting prejudicially against your employee over jury service (s 56(5))
      `what I did` IS A `What I did to my employee` @desc What you, or someone acting for you, did or would do to the employee
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can the court order me to take my employee back` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ someone who has been summonsed for jury service` THEN
        IF `I have been convicted under s 56(5)`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can the court order my re-employment` TRUE (`in the employee's words` `what I did`))
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 58B -- the fees`

@export Do I get the State's jury service fees for my employee (Juries Act 1957 (WA) s 58B(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my employee is employed on a contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employee is on a contract of service, not a contractor
      `I pay my employee their usual earnings for the jury service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you pay the employee the earnings they could reasonably expect for the period of jury service
      `I am in a prescribed class of employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations under the Act put you in a class of employer not entitled to the fees
      `my employee is in a prescribed class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations under the Act put the employee in a class not entitled to the fees
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Do I get the State's jury service fees for my employee` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ someone who has been summonsed for jury service` THEN `yes if` (`Who gets the jury service fees` `my employee is employed on a contract of service` `I pay my employee their usual earnings for the jury service` `I am in a prescribed class of employer` `my employee is in a prescribed class` EQUALS `my employer`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`
